---
const steps = [
  {
    title: 'Register the agent',
    body: 'Paste its A2A base URL. Guardrail Hub reads the Agent Card and fills in the name, description and skills.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Attach guardrails and limits',
    body: 'Pick guardrails and policies, set the order, add budgets and timeouts. Company-wide mandatory policies are already there.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Deploy a guarded URL',
    body: 'You get a new URL and an API key. Point your app at it instead of the agent.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Let people test it',
    body: 'Testers chat with the guarded agent and see, per message, which guardrails ran and what they did.',
  },
]
---

<section id="how" class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24 sm:px-6">
  <h2 class="max-w-2xl text-3xl leading-tight font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
    From agent URL to guarded URL in four steps.
  </h2>

  <ol class="mt-12 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-10 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4">
    {
      steps.map((step, i) => (
        <li class="border-t-2 border-ink pt-5">
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-muted">{i + 1}</span>
          <h3 class="mt-2 text-lg font-semibold">{step.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-2 leading-relaxed text-muted">{step.body}</p>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <div class="mt-20">
    <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold">What happens to each request</h3>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Mandatory policies run first and their blocks can’t be overridden. A block at either stage
      stops the call, and the agent never sees a blocked input.
    </p>

    <div class="path mt-10" role="img" aria-label="Request path: your app sends a message to the guarded URL. Input guardrails check it, then the agent answers, then output guardrails check the reply before it returns to your app. A block at the input stage returns a rejected task without calling the agent.">
      <div class="node">Your app</div>
      <div class="edge"></div>
      <div class="node node-check">
        Input guardrails
        <span>block, redact or warn</span>
      </div>
      <div class="edge"></div>
      <div class="node node-agent">
        Your agent
        <span>unchanged</span>
      </div>
      <div class="edge"></div>
      <div class="node node-check">
        Output guardrails
        <span>block, redact or warn</span>
      </div>
      <div class="edge"></div>
      <div class="node">Your app</div>

      <div class="branch">
        <span class="branch-line"></span>
        Blocked input returns <code>TASK_STATE_REJECTED</code> with the reason
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .path {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    row-gap: 0.75rem;
  }

  .node {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.125rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    border-radius: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px var(--color-line-strong);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .node span {
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .node-check {
    background: var(--color-teal-soft);
    box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgb(15 110 100 / 0.35);
    color: var(--color-teal-dark);
  }

  .node-agent {
    background: var(--color-ink);
    color: #fff;
    box-shadow: none;
  }

  .node-agent span {
    color: #a3a7ae;
  }

  .edge {
    height: 2px;
    min-width: 1.5rem;
    background: var(--color-ink);
    position: relative;
  }

  .edge::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    right: -1px;
    top: -4px;
    border: 5px solid transparent;
    border-left: 7px solid var(--color-ink);
    border-right: 0;
  }

  /* The block branch drops from the input guardrails node (column 3). */
  .branch {
    grid-column: 3 / -1;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-danger);
  }

  .branch-line {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    flex: none;
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 2px dashed var(--color-danger);
    border-bottom: 2px dashed var(--color-danger);
    border-bottom-left-radius: 0.5rem;
    margin-top: -1.25rem;
  }

  .branch code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    background: var(--color-danger-bg);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 0.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 960px) {
    .path {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      justify-items: start;
      row-gap: 0;
    }

    .edge {
      width: 2px;
      height: 1.5rem;
      min-width: 0;
      margin-left: 1.5rem;
    }

    .edge::after {
      right: -4px;
      top: auto;
      bottom: -1px;
      border: 5px solid transparent;
      border-top: 7px solid var(--color-ink);
      border-bottom: 0;
    }

    .branch {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: 4;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.25rem 0.375rem;
      margin: 0.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    }

    .branch-line {
      display: none;
    }

    .node {
      white-space: normal;
    }
  }
</style>
